{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d1f85d96b1c5a8656350efead33c7527ca19d0712b0ce654985ec086a80318c5","digest":{"component_or_area":"JiraConfig validation & initialization","key_entities":["JiraConfig","ReconcilerConfig","_validate_reconciler_tls","src/rebar/_config_schema.py","resolve_jira_settings","write_jira_config","InsecureUrlError","jira.url","jira.allow_insecure","REBAR_JIRA_ALLOW_INSECURE","_validate_https_url"],"problem_keywords":["cleartext credential exposure","https validation","jira config","insecure url","fail-loud validation"],"propositions":["JiraConfig accepts non-https jira.url silently, risking credential exposure in cleartext HTTP transit","Config load consumers (resolve_jira_settings, _jira_onboard._detect, write_jira_config) swallow ConfigError, allowing insecure URLs to bypass DC-style validation","ReconcilerConfig rejects non-https reconciler.base_url loudly unless allow_insecure is set, but JiraConfig has no equivalent __post_init__ validation","write_jira_config persists jira.url without scheme validation, so the onboarding wizard can silently write cleartext URLs to the config file","Parity fix requires: generalized _validate_https_url helper, JiraConfig.allow_insecure field, __post_init__ validation, fail-loud write path, and selective re-raise in resolve_jira_settings"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787543441525183001,"uuid":"9031fdb9-54e9-495a-842c-cc232e2296ae"}